{"name":"Neon Yellow","hex":"#cfff04","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"neon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The chemical element (symbol Ne) with an atomic number of 10. The second of the noble gases, it is a colourless, odorless inert gas.\n A form or sample of the element.","A form or sample of the element."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["That resembles a neon light; extremely bright; fluorescent"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/neon"},{"term":"yellow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of sunflower petals and lemons; the color obtained by mixing green and red light, or by subtracting blue from white light; the color evoked by light of wavelength around 580 nm; one of the three primary colors in subtractive color systems.","The middle light in a set of three traffic lights, the lighting of which indicates that drivers should stop short of the intersection if it is safe to do so."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a yellow hue.","Lacking courage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yellow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lemon (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lemon or lemon-color is a vivid yellow color characteristic of the lemon fruit. Shades of \"lemon\" may vary significantly from the fruit's actual color, including fluorescent tones and creamy hues reflective of lemon pies and confections."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Lemon_-_whole_and_split.jpg/330px-Lemon_-_whole_and_split.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lemon_(color)","wikidata":"Q2720565"},{"title":"Neon","blocks":[{"text":"Neon is a chemical element; it has the symbol Ne and the atomic number 10. It is the second noble gas in the periodic table. Neon is a colorless, odorless, inert monatomic gas under standard conditions, with approximately two-thirds the density of air."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Neon_discharge_tube.jpg/330px-Neon_discharge_tube.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neon","wikidata":"Q654"},{"title":"Yellow","blocks":[{"text":"Yellow is a color between green and orange on the spectrum of light. It is evoked by light with a dominant wavelength of roughly 575–585 nm. It is a primary color in subtractive color systems, used in painting or color printing. In the RGB color model, used to create colors on television and computer screens, yellow is a secondary color made by combining red and green at equal intensity. Carotenoids give the characteristic yellow color to autumn leaves, corn, canaries, daffodils, and lemons, as well as egg yolks, buttercups, and bananas. They absorb light energy and protect plants from photo damage in some cases. Sunlight has a slight yellowish hue when the Sun is near the horizon, due to atmospheric scattering of shorter wavelengths."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg/330px-Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow","wikidata":"Q943"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Lemon_tree_Italy.JPG/500px-Lemon_tree_Italy.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Lemon_tree_Italy.JPG/1280px-Lemon_tree_Italy.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Lemon_tree_Italy.JPG/500px-Lemon_tree_Italy.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A lemon tree in Italy","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALemon_tree_Italy.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Lemon_Chiffon_Cake.jpg/500px-Lemon_Chiffon_Cake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Lemon_Chiffon_Cake.jpg/500px-Lemon_Chiffon_Cake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A lemon chiffon cake","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALemon_Chiffon_Cake.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Lemon_Meringue_Pie.jpg/500px-Lemon_Meringue_Pie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Lemon_Meringue_Pie.jpg/1280px-Lemon_Meringue_Pie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Lemon_Meringue_Pie.jpg/500px-Lemon_Meringue_Pie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lemon meringue pie","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALemon_Meringue_Pie.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/NeTube.jpg/500px-NeTube.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/NeTube.jpg/1280px-NeTube.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/NeTube.jpg/500px-NeTube.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Neon gas-discharge lamps forming neon's element symbol","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANeTube.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Discovery_of_neon_isotopes.JPG/500px-Discovery_of_neon_isotopes.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Discovery_of_neon_isotopes.JPG/1280px-Discovery_of_neon_isotopes.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Discovery_of_neon_isotopes.JPG/500px-Discovery_of_neon_isotopes.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The first evidence for isotopes of a stable element was provided in 1913 by experiments on neon plasma. In the bottom right corner of J. J. Thomson's photographic plate are the separate impact marks for the two isotopes neon-20 and neon-22.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADiscovery_of_neon_isotopes.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Visible_spectrum_of_neon.jpg/500px-Visible_spectrum_of_neon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Visible_spectrum_of_neon.jpg/1280px-Visible_spectrum_of_neon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Visible_spectrum_of_neon.jpg/500px-Visible_spectrum_of_neon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The emission spectrum of neon shows individual wavelengths of light contributing to its perceived color when heated.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVisible_spectrum_of_neon.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Ne-water_clathrate.png/500px-Ne-water_clathrate.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Ne-water_clathrate.png/500px-Ne-water_clathrate.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Crystal structure of Ne clathrate hydrate[38]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANe-water_clathrate.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/FLOR